   "description": "Grief is the inner response to genuine loss — the pain of bereavement, devastation, and the experience of something or someone precious being gone. The Hebrew vocabulary is among the richest in the corpus, spanning the darkness of mourning, the bitterness of affliction, and the sorrow of a broken heart. God himself grieves in Scripture: he is grieved by the wickedness of humanity (Genesis 6), the breaking of the relationship he made. Grief is honoured in the Bible rather than suppressed; it is the appropriate inner response to a world where real loss happens.",
